-- a trigger needs table ownership, which no runtime role has (data §3.1). A nullable-account table
-- (data §2.4, plan 2.1): platform-only effects carry no account. Each insert statement notifies
-- the relay on channel elx_outbox; PostgreSQL delivers a NOTIFY only when the transaction commits,
-- so a rolled-back business change never wakes it (integrations §4.4).
--
-- core_consumer_receipts and core_consumer_dead_letters (data §2.1, §5.3): internal consumers'
-- receipts (35 days) and dead letters (30 days); their account mirrors the event's, so both are
-- nullable-account tables too. Neither references core_outbox: outbox rows are pruned after 7 days.
--
-- core_outbox_pending_id_idx serves the relay's batch, ORDER BY id over pending rows (data §5.2;
-- PLAT-8 lead review round 1); core_outbox_pending_due_idx serves the oldest-due-row alert query.
-- core_outbox_finished_idx and core_consumer_receipts_processed_idx serve the daily pruning job
-- across accounts (plan 2.8) and the platform list of dead rows (PLAT-8 item G).
--
